From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:57:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grt: BIG_INT is constexpr, so passing it by reference links
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mazeRouteMSMDOrder3D fills the distance grid with
std::fill_n(..., BIG_INT), which takes the value by const reference and
so ODR-uses FastRouteCore::BIG_INT. A `static const int` member with an
in-class initializer has no definition to bind to: the fastbuild link of
//:openroad fails with "undefined symbol: grt::FastRouteCore::BIG_INT"
(an optimized build inlines the fill and never needs one). A constexpr
static member is implicitly inline and carries its own definition.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h
index 13027d7..1572cf9 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FastRoute.h
@@ -886,7 +886,7 @@ class FastRouteCore
 
   using Tile = std::tuple<int, int, int>;
 
-  static const int BIG_INT = 1e9;  // big integer used as infinity
+  static constexpr int BIG_INT = 1e9;  // big integer used as infinity
   static const int HCOST = 5000;
   // Overflow an NDR net is charged, in its routing cost, per track it would
   // miss on an edge where it fits no single layer.
